<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Toru third-party notices</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 60rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1rem; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  ul.crates { columns: 2; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { background: #1e1e1e; color: #ddd; }
    a { color: #8ab4f8; }
    pre { background: #2a2a2a; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party notices</h1>
<p>Toru is built with the open-source Rust crates listed below, under the licences shown. The source code of each
crate is available from its crates.io page, linked from its name. The licences of the bundled fonts are in the
<code>licences\fonts</code> folder next to this file.</p>

<h2>Licences used</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

<h2>Licence texts</h2>
{{#each licenses}}
<section>
  <h3{{#if first_of_kind}} id="{{id}}"{{/if}}>{{name}}</h3>
  <p>Used by:</p>
  <ul class="crates">
  {{#each used_by}}
    <li><a href="https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}/{{crate.version}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
  {{/each}}
  </ul>
  <pre>{{text}}</pre>
</section>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
